+    "content": "# Result\n\nAll six positive exceptions are resolved conditionally within the declared action. For t=2/3, 8/3 and 16/(4±√2), use the exact S3 vertex-stabilizer sector and gradient seed. For t=16/(6±√2), use the C4 cyclic sector and cycle seed. Retained field frequencies avoid 2 and 4; the Coulomb-corrected averaged drift is nonzero in every case. Exact fixed-point invariance prevents nonlinear excitation of excluded modes along these witnesses.\n\nFixed species norms, exact initial Gauss constraints, a controlled O(1/epsilon) nonlinear comparison and a gauge-invariant higher-simplex population witness give nonlinear orbital departure. Together with prior NOI v0.1: all a>0, kappa>=0, finite r, alpha>0 for this nonzero flat family. Positive-stiffness vacuum stability is preserved. 104 exact checks; six numerical campaigns; no empirical evidence; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.\n\n# Six-case resonance closure v0.1\n\nUnder the unchanged candidate joint Hamiltonian, exact S3 and C4 fixed-point sectors provide nonlinear orbital instability witnesses at all six previously unresolved positive parameters. Combined with NOI v0.1, the specified nonzero neutral flat family is unstable for every a>0, kappa>=0 and finite rank. This is conditional mathematics, with independent review pending and physical promotion 0.\n\nRead `UD_RESONANCE_CLOSURE_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf`. Its TeX is the proof source. Reproduce the 104 exact constructor checks and six separately typed nonlinear numerical campaigns with `python3 verify_resonance_closure.py` (Python, SymPy, NumPy, SciPy). The graph constructor is unchanged from the preceding release. No experimental data or new action term is used.\n\n`CLAIM_AND_BRIDGE_LEDGER_v0.1.json` gives typed claims; `SOURCE_PROVENANCE_v0.1.json` records inherited dependency hashes. This release closes the six-case exception in NOI v0.1 without modifying its frozen artifacts. The all-parameter corollary additionally depends on that earlier proof. Other backgrounds, independent review and physical bridges remain open.\n"
